Z||000000||Art Doyle||12-20-2001||08:48 PM||||This has happened twice to my son's 1988 Fiero. Is this a design defect or indicative of some type of abnormal operation?<P>He does park the vehicle on a very steep slope, and we did have cold temperatures last night. The clutch, throwout bearing, and slave cylinder were replaced 2000 miles ago.||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-20-2001||11:42 PM||||This seems to be happening a lot lately.<P>Onset of cold weather seems to trigger hydraulic problems.  I'm guessing that old, marginally effective seals lose their resilience when cold -- like Challenger's booster o-rings.<P>See <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016441.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016441.html</A>  and other recent and past posts.<P>Good luck!  I had <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/015204.html" TARGET=_blank>my fight</A> with clutch hydraulics earlier.<BR>||||reg||1
